WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:22.000
Accessible forms
A form needs more than visual styling: every field needs a clear name and validation rules. Matching label for with input id connects them for assistive technology.

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:44.000
Explanation
A placeholder is not a label: it disappears when typing. type="email" enables basic format validation and required rejects an empty value.

00:00:44.000 --> 00:01:06.000
Trace the code
<form>
  <label for="email">Email</label>
  <input id="email" name="email" type="email" required>
  <button type="submit">Send</button>
</form>

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:28.000
Result
email

for="email" must match id="email".

00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:50.000
Remember
Browser validation does not replace server validation. This example teaches structure; no submission backend is attached.
